{
  "slug": "chrome-devtools-mcp",
  "name": "Chrome Devtools Mcp",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Control and inspect a live Chrome browser from your coding agent. Record performance traces, analyze network requests, check console messages with source-mapped stack traces, and automate browser actions with Puppeteer.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `a11y-debugging` (Uses Chrome DevTools MCP for accessibility (a11y) debugging and auditing based on web.dev guidelines), `chrome-devtools` (Uses Chrome DevTools via MCP for efficient debugging, troubleshooting and browser automation), `chrome-devtools-cli` (Use this skill to write shell scripts or run shell commands to automate tasks in the browser or…), `debug-optimize-lcp` (Guides debugging and optimizing Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) using Chrome DevTools MCP tools), `memory-leak-debugging` (Diagnoses and resolves memory leaks in JavaScript/Node.js applications), `troubleshooting` (Uses Chrome DevTools MCP and documentation to troubleshoot connection and target issues)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `chrome-devtools`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install chrome-devtools-mcp@claude-plugins-official` from `ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 7,
    "mcp": 1
  },
